 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "DURApulse GS3 AC Drives User Manual - Chapter 5: GS3 Modbus Communications",
  "doc_number": "GS3-M 2nd Edition (chapter 5)",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://cdn.automationdirect.com/static/manuals/gs3m/ch5.pdf",
  "pages": "Comm parameter summary pp. 5-2 to 5-3; parameter addresses pp. 5-4 to 5-8; status addresses pp. 5-9 to 5-11; example message near the end of the chapter"
 },
 "notes": [
  "AutomationDirect's own manual chapter (cdn.automationdirect.com).",
  "Parameter-to-register rule: Px.yy is at hex x*256 + yy (e.g. P9.26 = 091Ah = 42331); the full list is in the chapter's parameter address tables. Only the P9 communication/control parameters are included here.",
  "Status values marked XXX.X in the manual carry one implied decimal (scale 0.1).",
  "Scale Frequency is split into low word (2108h) and high word (2109h), so it is listed as a 32-bit value with the low word first (CDAB); its unit depends on P8.01.",
  "P9.05 (communication time-out, 0.1-60.0 s) is left out because its raw encoding is not stated in this chapter.",
  "The factory protocol (P9.02 = 0) is Modbus ASCII 7N2; set 3, 4 or 5 for RTU.",
  "Speed reference scaling: the manual's example frame 01 10 09 1B 00 02 04 02 58 00 01 writes 0258h (600) for 60 Hz; it starts at 091Bh although the table puts P9.26 at 091Ah (42331). The table address is used here.",
  "Left out: Output Current (2104h), Power Factor Angle (210Ah) and PID setpoint/feedback (210Ch/210Dh) because no decimal format is given for them.",
  "P9.01 baud codes are not readable in the chapter's summary table; the setup example uses 01 = 9600 baud.",
  "The P9.00/P9.01 rows of the chapter's summary table are not readable, so their factory defaults are not given here."
 ],
